# Open-source privacy

Before finishing any edit in this repo, run `./scripts/check-privacy.sh`.

- Do not add company brand names, company domains, or internal hostnames.
- Do not use real employees as examples, seeds, fixtures, or CI users.
- Allowed demo identity: `张伟` / `Alex.Zhang` / `alex.zhang@example.com`.
- Allowed generic emails: `admin@example.com`, `name@example.com`.
- Put new forbidden terms only in `scripts/privacy-denylist.txt`.
- Do not copy private drill hosts, backups, or git history into the public tree.
